{#
  Timeline: a marker per entry on a connecting line, the kind of change in bold, what changed
  underneath, and the status in plain text where the entry is settled. An entry with no status
  renders with a hollow marker and no status text, so an open item reads as open at a glance.
  Originally built for Policy writer v2's chapter history; shared here since Gateway 2's chapter
  audit log needs the same shape.

  Usage (caller decides ordering, e.g. newest-first via the `reverse` filter, and supplies its
  own heading — this macro renders only the list itself):
    {% from "partials/timeline/macro.njk" import appTimeline %}
    {{ appTimeline({ entries: chapter.history | reverse }) }}

  params.entries: array of { type, description, date, actor, status? } — status is optional;
    when present the entry's marker fills in and the status text shows, e.g. "Done".
  params.caption: string (optional) — defaults to a stock "this is example content" caveat,
    since every consumer so far is read-only illustrative content rather than a real log.
#}

{% macro appTimeline(params) %}
<ol class="app-timeline">
  {% for entry in params.entries %}
    <li class="app-timeline__entry{% if entry.status %} app-timeline__entry--done{% endif %}">
      <span class="app-timeline__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <p class="app-timeline__head">
        <span class="app-timeline__type">{{ entry.type }}</span>
        {% if entry.status %}
          <span class="app-timeline__status">{{ entry.status }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </p>

      <p class="app-timeline__text">{{ entry.description }}</p>
      <p class="app-timeline__meta">{{ entry.date }} &middot; {{ entry.actor }}</p>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>

<p class="app-timeline__caption">{{ params.caption | default("Example history — this prototype does not record your changes.") }}</p>
{% endmacro %}
